## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of encryption, key management, cross-account access, and operational rotation at scale with compliance demands.

## Key Concepts

- Envelope encryption
- KMS CMKs and data keys
- Key rotation strategies
- Background re-encryption of existing data
- IAM/bucket policies per tenant
- Auditability with CloudTrail

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: rotate tenant data keys
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const kms = new AWS.KMS();
async function rotateTenantDataKey(cmkArn) {
  const { CiphertextBlob, Plaintext } = await kms.generateDataKey({ KeyId: cmkArn, KeySpec: 'AES_256' }).promise();
  // Store CiphertextBlob in tenant metadata; use Plaintext to encrypt new data in memory (do not persist plaintext)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test rotation in CI/CD without impacting production?
- How do you handle key revocation and tenant offboarding while preserving audits?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region, multi-account DR with strict IAM boundaries and automated failover.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-region replication (S3 CRR, DynamoDB Global Tables)
- Route 53 failover with health checks
- Per-tenant IAM roles with least privilege and explicit denies
- IaC automation and DR testing

## Code Example

```terraform
# Minimal Terraform snippet for Route53 failover
resource "aws_route53_health_check" "region_a" {
  fqdn = "api.example.com"
  type = "HTTPS"
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "primary" {
  name = "api.example.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = var.zone_id
  set_identifier = "RegionA"
  failover_routing_policy {
    type = "primary"
    health_check_id = aws_route53_health_check.region_a.id
  }
  alias {
    name = aws_lb.region_a.dns_name
    zone_id = aws_lb.region_a.zone_id
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "secondary" {
  name = "api.example.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = var.zone_id
  set_identifier = "RegionB"
  failover_routing_policy {
    type = "secondary"
    health_check_id = aws_route53_health_check.region_b.id
  }
  alias {
    name = aws_lb.region_b.dns_name
    zone_id = aws_lb.region_b.zone_id
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify data consistency after failover?
- What monitoring alerts would you add?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design scalable, auditable data-lake isolation using Lake Formation, IAM tagging, and cross-account roles; also assesses policy drafting and test planning.

## Key Concepts

- Lake Formation permissions and data location mapping
- IAM tags and condition keys
- Cross-account roles and trust policies
- S3 tenant prefixes and data encryption with KMS
- Admin audit paths and automated tests

## Code Example

```json
{
  "PolicySnippet": {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
        "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-id/*",
        "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "LFPolicySnippet": {
    "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantRole"},
    "Permissions": ["SELECT","DESCRIBE","ALTER"],
